# fog.js Editing Rules

## Structure
fog.js is one large IIFE. Key sections in order:
1. Constants & state variables
2. Canvas / Leaflet setup
3. Canvas click handler (lines ~310-430) — contains isClickable() call + golden-glow bypass
4. Tutorial system (advanceTutorial, TUTORIAL_DEFS)
5. Path logic (getNextPathLocation, isOnPath, isClickable)
6. draw() loop — section 3 (golden glow), section 3b (orange/yellow beacons), section 4 (clear holes)
7. Discovery system (instantDiscover, startSearchMode, completeDiscovery)
8. Guide Me button (addGuideButton, runGuideMe)

## Critical Functions — Do Not Break
- `isClickable(locId)` — gating logic, must match beacon draw proximity exactly
- `getNextPathLocation()` — iterates journeyPath, returns first undiscovered step ID
- `draw()` — RAF loop, don't add expensive operations inside it
- `completeDiscovery(loc)` — clears searchMode, triggers fog reveal

## After Every Edit
```bash
node --check fog.js
```

## Common Patterns

### Proximity check (standard 400-unit gate):
```js
var nearCleared = false;
Object.keys(discovered).forEach(function(dId) {
  if (nearCleared) return;
  var dLoc = allLocs.find(function(l) { return l.id === dId; });
  if (!dLoc) return;
  var dx = loc.lat - dLoc.lat, dy = loc.lng - dLoc.lng;
  if (Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy) < 400) nearCleared = true;
});
```

### Find location by ID:
```js
var loc = (window.LOCATIONS || []).find(function(l) { return l.id === 'some-id'; });
```

### Convert map coord to screen pixel:
```js
var pt = map.latLngToContainerPoint([loc.lat, loc.lng]);
```
